        "filename": "Mauna Loa Observatory.jpg",
        "caption": "This natural-colour satellite image of the summit of Mauna Loa — overlaid with 100-meter contour lines, helps illustrate why volcanic emissions from the summit rarely reach the observatory. \nThe observatory is located on the northern slope of the mountain, 6 kilometres away from and 800 meters lower than the summit.\nMost of the time, the prevailing north-easterly trade winds prevent volcanically contaminated air from reaching the observatory. Only on a small percentage of nights do the winds become light and southerly, pushing volcanic emissions downhill to the observatory.",
